  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Raju @ Rajendra Kumar S/O Shri Gordhan ... vs State Of Rajasthan on 6 February, 2019 High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Miscellaneous (Petition) No. 870/2019 Raju @ Rajendra Kumar S/o Shri Gordhan Das B/c Sindhi, R/o 1- Gh-31, Dadabari, Kota, District Kota, Raj., Establishment Ganesh Family Shop No.3, Plot No.787, Shastri Nagar, Dadabari Kota, District Kota, Raj. ----Petitioner Versus 1. State Of Rajasthan, Through Pp. 2. Food Inspector Bundi, Chief Medical And Health Officer, Bundi, District Bundi, Raj. ----Respondents For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Jitendra Bajaj For Respondent(s) : Mr. N.S. Dhakad, Pp Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Kanwaljit Singh Ahluwalia Order 06/02/2019 Present petition has been filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C. praying that the proceedings arising out of criminal case No.442/2006 titled State of Rajasthan vs Raju @ Rajendra Kumar & Ors., pending in the court of Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate Bundi , under Section 7 read with Section 16 of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, be dropped inter alia on the following grounds:- ( a) That in the present case, complaint was filed after period of three years, hence, the same is barred under Section 468 Cr.P.C. (b) That in the present case, trial is being conducted by Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate Bundi, and he is not competent court to Raju @ Rajendra Kumar S/O Shri Gordhan ... vs State Of Rajasthan on 6 February, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175959443/",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "] try the offence as per Section 16(A) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954.",
